    # --- Guide (in the management program and in setup) ----------------------------
    'Guide.Intro'                    = @(
        '# How WePrintEasy works'
        'A fixed default printer is stored here for each employee (or each AD group). At every logon to the terminal server - and every time a disconnected session is reconnected - a small background process (the logon agent) sets exactly this printer as the default and keeps it there. Employees do not have to install or configure anything.'
        ''
    )
    'Guide.Server'                   = @(
        '## Part 1 - Setup on the terminal server (once, administrator)'
        '- Copy the WePrintEasy folder to the terminal server and double-click Setup.cmd (asks for administrator rights).'
        '- Choose the language and where to store the configuration: "This server only" - or, with several terminal servers, a share on the file server, e.g. \\fs01\WePrintEasy$\config.json (permissions: Domain Users read, administrators modify).'
        '- Enter the print/file server and click "Load printers": all shared printers appear. Preselected are those whose driver is already installed on this terminal server.'
        '- Optionally tick "Install missing drivers now" - important, because since the PrintNightmare updates normal users are not allowed to install printer drivers.'
        '- Confirm the options and click "Install". With several terminal servers, run setup on each server and specify the same share.'
        '- Then open the tab "Setup check" in the management program: all items should be "OK".'
        '> You will then find the management program in the Start menu under Windows Tools > "WePrintEasy Printer Management".'
        ''
    )
    'Guide.Assign'                   = @(
        '## Part 2 - Assign printers'
        '- Tab "Assignments" > "Assign user...".'
        '- Enter a name, click "Search", click the employee in the list.'
        '- Choose a printer from the list (this is the printer list from the file server) and click "Save".'
        '- For whole departments: "Assign group..." with an AD group. A user assignment always takes precedence; if someone is in several groups, the lowest priority number wins.'
        '- To check: tab "Check user" > "Resolve" shows which printer will be set at the next logon.'
        '- New printers on the file server? Tab "Printer list" > "Update from print/file server...".'
        '> Changes take effect immediately: employees who are already logged on get the new printer within about 30 seconds - without logging on again.'
        ''
    )
    'Guide.User'                     = @(
        '## Part 3 - On the employee''s side'
        '- Nothing needs to be installed or configured.'
        '- After the installation, SIGN OUT once and sign in again (Start > user > Sign out). Just closing the window or "Disconnect" is not enough the first time.'
        '- From then on, the assigned printer is automatically the default printer - also after reconnecting from home or from another PC.'
        '- If the employee sets a different default printer, it is reset after a short time (can be switched off in the "Settings" tab). Printing once on another printer is always possible via the print dialog.'
        '- Using printers of their own PC (e.g. home office): leave "Local Resources" > "Printers" ticked in Remote Desktop Connection and use a wildcard in the assignment, e.g. Brother*(redirected*.'
        ''
    )
    'Guide.Troubleshooting'          = @(
        '## Troubleshooting'
        '- Tab "Setup check": fix yellow and red items.'
        '- Printer is not set for an employee? Select the assignment > "Enforce now...": sets the printer immediately in their session on the terminal server and shows every step live - and where it fails (e.g. WePrintEasy not installed there, different configuration, no agent in the session, printer missing).'
        '- Tab "Check user" > "Show log": shows what the agent did for this employee, e.g. "Default printer set: ... (previously: ...)" - this also shows you what changed the printer.'
        '- "Printer is not (yet) available": share name wrong, file server not reachable or driver missing - update the printer list with "Install missing drivers".'
        '- Group membership changed in AD? Only takes effect after the employee signs out and in again.'
        '- Test the agent in your own session: tab "Setup check" > "Run agent for me now" or in PowerShell:'
        '$ powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "C:\Program Files\WePrintEasy\WePrintEasy-Agent.ps1" -Once -Verbose'
        '- Log file per user: %LOCALAPPDATA%\WePrintEasy\agent.log'
    )

